  "schema": "aicad.copilot_modes/1",
  "contract": "contracts/copilot_modes.md",
  "consumers": [
    "services/agent/copilot_mode_tools.py (Python: MCP/DAG agent_turn.run_turn gating)",
    "core/agent/copilot_modes.cpp (C++: in-app run.cpp mode gating)"
  ],
  "notes": [
    "Canonical per-mode tool allowlists for the Agent|Plan|Swarm|Edit|Ask copilot modes. The .md is the prose contract (mode semantics); this file is the machine-readable data BOTH runtimes load at runtime.",
    "Runtime resolution: C++ core/agent/copilot_modes.cpp honors CHUDWARE_COPILOT_MODES_JSON (explicit file) then CHUDWARE_CONTRACTS_DIR/<name> then the repo-relative contracts/copilot_modes.json (same CWD convention as core/agent/roles.cpp's services/agent/prompts fallback). Python services/agent/copilot_mode_tools.py honors CHUDWARE_COPILOT_MODES_JSON then <repo>/contracts/copilot_modes.json via Path(__file__).parents[2].",
    "mode_tools has no services/agent/swarm entry: those modes are unrestricted at the mode layer (unrestricted_modes) and a concrete list cannot express 'full catalog'.",
    "mutating_tools is the deny set applied to open-ended role cards in plan mode AND to ask mode; edit_denied is the extra deny set for edit mode; shared_default_tools is the floor UNIONed onto every restricted mode AFTER denylists (shared wins: new_part/close_part/import_part stay available in plan/ask/edit).",
    "Parity is enforced by core/tests/test_copilot_modes.cpp (doctest) and services/agent/test_copilot_modes_parity.py (pytest) over the same mode x tool verdict matrix.",
    "agent_default_tools is the always-on MAIN-agent loadout UNIONed onto the advertised list AND the dispatch policy for the unrestricted modes (services/agent/swarm) even when a role card narrows the list — file handling and web research stay available without burning context on rare CAD packs. Shell remains available only through explicit role/category enablement. subagent_default_tools is the file-handling floor UNIONed onto every DAG-node/subagent role loadout. Neither floor applies to ask/plan/edit (those keep their read-only fs floor via shared_default_tools). Rare families stay behind enable_tools/list_tool_categories."
  ],
